DolphinXR changes to DolRecomp fa0cf619e8d7eb8cba7eaf55267a12caaebb46aa for Wii REL modules
(Mario Kart Wii's StaticR.rel), applied with: git -C <DolRecomp> apply <this file>

- 16-bit REL relocations (ADDR16, _LO, _HI, _HA) patch the halfword at the relocation's offset,
  as the SDK's OSLink does; they were written 2 bytes further, over the next instruction.
- --rel-bss <addr>: the BSS address a game gives a single REL (allocated apart from it).
- An executable section off the REL's alignment is a warning: the OS aligns the module only.
- --direct-calls: cross-chunk calls run directly once the runtime says the target chunk is ready
  (int dolrecomp_chunk_ready(u32 chunk_start)); --extern-chunks <generated.h> lets a REL call
  main.dol's chunks the same way.
- Beside a REL's code: rel_layout.txt (header fields, section addresses) and rel_image.dol (the
  relocated code as a DOL at its address), which Tools/StaticRecomp/module-template consumes.
- --inline-cache-ops: dcbst/dcbf/dcbi/icbi call ppc_cache_control in line (Dolphin's cycle
  costs) instead of an interpreter fallback that ends the block; native code goes back to the
  dispatcher only when the environment's hook moves ctx->pc off the instruction (it does when the
  op invalidated a recompiled chunk) or the op raised an exception.
- dolrecomp_f32_from_bits (lfs, psq_l): a normal single converts as the host converts it, in
  line; zero, denormal, infinity and NaN take the bit-level conversion out of line. Identical
  results for all 2^32 inputs.
- --function-chunks (C backend): a chunk -- one C function -- per guest function, from the
  direct call targets (bl, bcl), several per C file. With --direct-calls, guest calls and returns
  become host calls and returns: call sites name the target chunk by its index in the module
  (int dolrecomp_chunk_ready_at(u32 index, u32 chunk_start)), branches into another chunk run it
  directly, indirect calls go through int dolrecomp_call_indirect(CPUState*, u32 target), a bctr
  into its own function goes back through the function's entry switch, and the call guard is a
  stack floor (char* dolrecomp_stack_floor) instead of a depth count. The dispatch lookup is the
  indexed one with 256-byte pages, and generated.h lists the covered code as
  // DOLRECOMP_CODE_RANGE lines.

